@reporter I am hitting:
TypeError: participant8() got an unexpected keyword argument 'participant9_meta'

Not sure if it is due to my PT2/Triton version.

I can reproduce the LLVM -> PTX locally.

Using LLVM at 49af6502c6dcb4a7f7520178bd14df396f78240c:

```
$ llc -march=nvptx64 < test.llir
```

[Download test.llir](https://github.com/openai/participant9/files/13385523/test.ll.txt)

This gives me the following PTX.  Because it's taking the f16 values from shmem and bitcasting them to f32, I don't see how this can be correct.  Unless maybe I'm misreading the shufflevector in LLVM and it's actually UB?  But it really *looks* fine.

